Darn.  Sorry, Jerry, I misplaced your email address.  The fix you mailed
me made my mac hang.  [ Apparently LSC4.0 waits on readchar() until a
key is pressed. :-( So it never leaves that loop.]  Here is the fix:

**************************************************************************
*  Make the yn() function clear the type-ahead buffer first.
*  This could save a few accidental quits, overeatings, etc.
*
*  From:  David C. Blume and Jerry D. Hedden
**************************************************************************

File:  topl.c
After line 279:
        addtopl(rtmp);
Add:
#ifdef MACOS
	FlushEvents(keyDownMask,0);  /* mac clear key buffer */
#else
	while(readchar());           /* other clear key buffer */
#endif

--David
